>## The natural (base-e) logarithm. log(1) = +0; log(+0) = log(-0) = -∞ (with division-by-zero exception in IEEE 754); log(x) for x < 0 is NaN (with invalid-operation exception); log(+∞) = +∞; log(NaN) is NaN.
