>
>## Numeric subtraction.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>##
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Constraint-polymorphic subtraction over any type with a 'numeric' instance. The per-type semantics live in the instance: two's-complement wraparound for fixed-width integers (e.g. int32 subtraction reduces x - y modulo 2^32 and reinterprets as signed, wrapping silently on overflow), IEEE 754 round-to-nearest for floating-point, and arbitrary precision for bigint.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Requires a 'numeric' type-class constraint on the argument type.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## The operation is total. Corresponds to Haskell's (-) :: Num a => a -> a -> a.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Generalized from int32-only; the numeric class is #566.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>##
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @availableSince 0.17.6
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#                  ^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @requirement wrapsOrRoundsPerType sub computes the difference of two values of a numeric type per that type's own arithmetic: two's-complement wraparound for fixed-width integers, arbitrary precision for bigint, IEEE 754 round-to-nearest for floating-point -- and dispatches correctly regardless of which numeric type is supplied at the call site.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @requirement boundaryWraparoundAndIeeeSpecialValues sub wraps silently at every fixed-width integer type's boundary; sub on bigint beyond int64/uint64 range remains exact; sub on float64/float32 follows IEEE 754 special-value rules (subtracting same-sign infinities or any NaN operand yields NaN, the difference of two equal finite values is +0, ties round to even).
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>primitive sub : ∀x.(numeric x) ⇒ x → x → x
#^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra keyword.other.definition.hydra
#         ^ source.hydra
#          ^^^ source.hydra entity.name.function.hydra
#             ^ source.hydra
#              ^ source.hydra punctuation.separator.type.hydra
#               ^ source.hydra
#                ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.forall-scheme.hydra
#                 ^ source.hydra variable.parameter.hydra
#                  ^ source.hydra punctuation.separator.binder.hydra
#                   ^ source.hydra
#                    ^^^^^^^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
#                           ^ source.hydra
#                            ^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
#                             ^^ source.hydra
#                               ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.constraint-arrow.hydra
#                                ^ source.hydra
#                                 ^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
#                                  ^ source.hydra
#                                   ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.arrow.hydra
#                                    ^ source.hydra
#                                     ^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
#                                      ^ source.hydra
#                                       ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.arrow.hydra
#                                        ^ source.hydra
#                                         ^ source.hydra variable.other.hydra
>
>## Floating-point subtraction.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>##
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## IEEE 754 binary64 subtraction, defined as x + (-y). The result is correctly rounded to the nearest representable float64 under roundTiesToEven.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Subtracting infinities of the same sign (+∞ - +∞ or -∞ - -∞) produces a NaN; subtracting any value involving NaN produces a NaN. The difference of two equal finite values is +0 (or -0 under round-toward-negative, which is not the default).
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## The operation is total: it never raises, but it may produce NaN. Corresponds to the IEEE 754 ੵ.4.1 subtraction operation and to Haskell's (-) :: Double -> Double -> Double.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## Deprecated since 0.18. Use: hydra.core.lib.math.sub.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>##
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @deprecatedSince 0.18
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#                   ^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>## @requirement subtractsFloat64Values subFloat64 computes the IEEE 754 binary64 difference of its two arguments.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#   ^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra keyword.other.documentation.directive.hydra
#               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>primitive subFloat64 : ∀.float64 → float64 → float64
#^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra keyword.other.definition.hydra
#         ^ source.hydra
#          ^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.function.hydra
#                    ^ source.hydra
#                     ^ source.hydra punctuation.separator.type.hydra
#                      ^ source.hydra
#                       ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.forall-scheme.hydra
#                        ^ source.hydra punctuation.separator.binder.hydra
#                         ^^^^^^^ source.hydra support.type.hydra
#                                ^ source.hydra
#                                 ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.arrow.hydra
#                                  ^ source.hydra
#                                   ^^^^^^^ source.hydra support.type.hydra
#                                          ^ source.hydra
#                                           ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.arrow.hydra
#                                            ^ source.hydra
#                                             ^^^^^^^ source.hydra support.type.hydra
